WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.060 --> 00:00:08.860
As ego driven individuals, we love to think
that the universe is all about us.

00:00:08.860 --> 00:00:14.410
That we are at the center and everything that
happens, happens because the universe has

00:00:14.410 --> 00:00:17.380
some divine plan for us.

00:00:17.380 --> 00:00:22.710
We are compelled to believe that the universe
personally cares about us.

00:00:22.710 --> 00:00:25.310
Otherwise, what is the point?

00:00:25.310 --> 00:00:30.980
How can we care about the universe if it does
not care about us?

00:00:30.980 --> 00:00:36.370
But just because we need it to care, does
not mean that it does.

00:00:36.370 --> 00:00:43.120
The universe or a god, as some might view
it, is not a human, nor does it function like

00:00:43.120 --> 00:00:44.470
one.

00:00:44.470 --> 00:00:47.260
It does not experience emotion or empathy.

00:00:47.260 --> 00:00:55.920
And it does not care about the ways in which
humans perceive and experience what it is.

00:00:55.920 --> 00:00:57.150
It functions objectively.

00:00:57.150 --> 00:01:03.920
And therefore, fundamentally, things do not
happen for a reason.

00:01:03.920 --> 00:01:09.920
They happen merely because of the arbitrary
alignments of time and space.

00:01:09.920 --> 00:01:12.829
Mere coincidence.

00:01:12.829 --> 00:01:19.200
But then why does it so often seem that when
things happen, they happen for a reason?

00:01:19.200 --> 00:01:25.929
That every time something happens to us, it
leads to some purpose in our life.

00:01:25.929 --> 00:01:32.350
That even when bad things happen to us, they
can end up leading us to good things.

00:01:32.350 --> 00:01:38.850
Certainly there must be a reason why the cliché,
“everything happens for a reason,” is

00:01:38.850 --> 00:01:41.829
so widely popular.

00:01:41.829 --> 00:01:50.159
The real reason is because of the resilience
of human nature and the power of our imaginations.

00:01:50.159 --> 00:01:56.880
Things appear to happen for a reason not because
the universe or a god-like figure is watching

00:01:56.880 --> 00:02:05.100
over us, playing us like a prewritten video
game, but because as humans, we have the power

00:02:05.100 --> 00:02:09.250
to MAKE things happen for a reason.

00:02:09.250 --> 00:02:15.200
When things happen to us, we assimilate them
into our life and give them a reason for being

00:02:15.200 --> 00:02:16.870
there.

00:02:16.870 --> 00:02:23.780
We perceive the alignments of time and space
and attach narratives and purpose to the things

00:02:23.780 --> 00:02:25.920
that occur.

00:02:25.920 --> 00:02:28.200
We are the writers of our own story.

00:02:28.200 --> 00:02:35.030
For every moment we experience, we have the
ability to write our own meaning.

00:02:35.030 --> 00:02:42.150
For every conflict we face, we have the ability
to write our own resolution.

00:02:42.150 --> 00:02:51.100
We can learn, adapt, and create purpose out
of the randomness of life within the universe.

00:02:51.100 --> 00:02:58.019
And in my opinion, that is even more comforting
than the idea that things happen for some

00:02:58.019 --> 00:03:26.959
ulterior reason.

